From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:01:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): search, filter and group the Open items panel

A coordinator session raises tens of items across several pieces of work,
and the Open items panel lists them in one column by status, so finding
the open risks of one topic means reading the whole list.

Once the panel holds five items or more it gets a search box and one row
of chips: Open, Answered and Closed with counts, the kinds present and the
topics in use. The search matches every typed word in an item's label,
title, detail or topic; a chip keeps one status, kind or topic, and each
count is what selecting it would list. Items group by status (as before),
topic or kind, each group folding from its heading; the grouping is kept
in this browser, and the search, chips and folds survive the panel closing
until the page reloads. On a phone the search stays first in the sheet and
the chips scroll sideways in one row. Filtering runs over the loaded list,
which the store caps at 500 items, so it needs nothing from the server.

Not proposed upstream yet: the panel it extends is not upstream either.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
